From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:00:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: detile all MTK tile rows on Midgard and Bifrost

panfrost_mtk_detile_compute() reads each tiled plane through a linear
image view with one row per tile, so the source view holds
(pitch / tile width) x (tile rows) rows. On Midgard and Bifrost,
emit_image_bufs() bounds image accesses with the attribute buffer's T
dimension, which it takes from the resource's height0: the picture
height. The detile then stops after height0 tiles, and everything past
them stays tiled. A 1920x1080 H.264 frame on a Mali-T880 is correct for
the first 1080 luma tiles (288 rows) and 540 chroma tiles, and garbled
below.

Expose the full tile row count in height0 while the detile job is
emitted, and restore it afterwards. Valhall images take their size from
the image layout and are not affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
index bcb3abe..4ba5093 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
@@ -3957,6 +3957,19 @@ panfrost_mtk_detile_compute(struct panfrost_context *ctx, struct pipe_blit_info
          DIV_ROUND_UP(uv_src->height0, 16);
    }
 
+   /* Midgard and Bifrost bound image accesses by the S/T dimensions of the
+    * attribute buffer, which emit_image_bufs() takes from width0/height0.
+    * The tiled sources are linear views with one row per tile, so height0
+    * (the picture height) would stop the detile after height0 tiles. Expose
+    * all tile rows while the job is emitted. */
+   unsigned y_src_height0 = y_src ? y_src->height0 : 0;
+   unsigned uv_src_height0 = uv_src ? uv_src->height0 : 0;
+
+   if (y_src)
+      y_src->height0 = pan_resource(y_src)->image.props.extent_px.height;
+   if (uv_src)
+      uv_src->height0 = pan_resource(uv_src)->image.props.extent_px.height;
+
    image[0].resource = y_src;
    image[0].format = PIPE_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UINT;
    image[0].shader_access = image[0].access = PIPE_IMAGE_ACCESS_READ;
@@ -4028,6 +4041,11 @@ panfrost_mtk_detile_compute(struct panfrost_context *ctx, struct pipe_blit_info
    panfrost_resource_restore_format(pan_resource(uv_src), &uv_src_save);
    panfrost_resource_restore_format(pan_resource(y_dst), &y_dst_save);
    panfrost_resource_restore_format(pan_resource(uv_dst), &uv_dst_save);
+
+   if (y_src)
+      y_src->height0 = y_src_height0;
+   if (uv_src)
+      uv_src->height0 = uv_src_height0;
 }
 
 static void *
